5.8 Techniques
•	Data preparation
•	Converting non-numerical data into numerical data (one-hot encoding)
•	Converting invalid dates to NaN (errors="coerce")
•	Removing rows with NaN
•	Model training 
o	Supervised machine learning approach
o	Use a regression algorithm
o	Linear regression: models the relationship between multiple input features and sales amount using a linear equation
•	Train/test split
•	Saving the trained model (joblib)
•	Loading a saved model (joblib)
•	Checking that required files exist before running
•	Collecting user input (numbers, date, menu choices)
•	Input validation (invalid date, invalid menu choices)
•	Matching the new data to the model's features (reindex)
•	Predicting with model.predict()
       Split Type
•	Train/test split (hold-out method) using train_test_split
•	60% training / 40% testing (test_size=0.40)
•	Random split with random_state=42 for reproducible results
•	Done in the training script only; the prediction tool does no splitting
5.9 Evaluation Metrics
•	R² Score
•	Mean Absolute Error (MAE)
•	Root Mean Squared Error (RMSE)
•	Actual vs Predicted Sales Amount scatter plot (made with matplotlib)
•	Calculated in the training script only; the prediction tool only makes predictions
